# Group-scoped tRPC procedures

## Slug, not groupId

- Group procedures take `{ slug: string }` (plus other fields) in the input.
- Resolve `group` from the slug in middleware / procedure helpers.
- **Never** accept a bare `groupId` from the client body as the tenancy key.
- Use `ctx.group.id` after resolution for DB writes.

## Procedure stack (`src/TRPC/init.ts`)

| Procedure | Requirements |
|---|---|
| `groupProcedure` | Authed + group exists (hidden → only active members) |
| `groupMemberProcedure` | Active membership |
| `groupModeratorProcedure` | Role `moderator` \| `admin` \| `owner` |
| `groupAdminProcedure` | Role `admin` \| `owner` |
| `groupOwnerProcedure` | Role `owner` |

`ctx.group` and `ctx.membership` are injected after the guard runs.

## Contracts

Shared Zod + serializers live in `@repo/api` (`membership.ts`, `MEMBERSHIP_T_MESSAGES`).
